error[R0605] (conservative): `for` from `#items` down to 1 without a `-1` step
--> 12:10: starts at `#items` and counts UP (the step is +1)
  = note: counting up from a length to 1, the body never runs when the table holds more than one element — a reverse walk needs an explicit `-1` step
  = note: valid Luau — deliberate only if the table is known to hold at most one element
  = help: make the step negative: `-1`
          -1

error[R0605] (conservative): `for` from `#items` down to 0 without a `-1` step
--> 21:10: starts at `#items` and counts UP (the default step is +1)
  = note: counting up from a length to 0, the body runs only for an empty table — and then the index is 0, which no array holds
  = note: valid Luau — deliberate only if the table is known to be empty
  = help: add the step: `0, -1`
          0, -1
